YouTube Transcript API with Search, Channels & Playlists | TranscriptAPI TranscriptAPI.com Docs Pricing Blog Contact Login Get API Key YouTube Transcript API That Just Works Stop fighting YouTube blocks. Get transcripts, search videos, browse channels, and extract playlists via REST API or YouTube MCP — at scale. Get Started Free View Pricing Works everywhere Powering 15M+ transcripts every month Your browser does not support the video tag. Trusted in production 500K+ Transcripts Processed Daily 49ms median response time. 15M+ transcripts served last month. youtubetotranscript.com Verified Production User ~11M transcripts per month Active recapio.com Verified Production User ~2.8M transcripts per month Active Everything you need from YouTube One API. Full YouTube Access. Transcripts, search, channels, playlists — all in one place. Every feature works via API, MCP, and agent skills. Get Transcripts 1 credit Extract transcripts from any YouTube video — with or without timestamps. Drop the output straight into summarizers, search indexes, or AI pipelines. Summarize videos Study notes Search indexes Content repurposing Request Copy curl " https://transcriptapi.com/api/v2/youtube/transcript?video_url=dQw4w9WgXcQ&format=json " \ -H " Authorization: Bearer API_KEY " Response {
  " language ": " en ",
  " length_seconds ": 1164 ,
  " lengthText ": " 19:24 ",
  " metadata ": {
    " title ": " Do schools kill creativity? "
  },
  " transcript ": [
    {
      " text ": " Good morning. How are you? ",
      " start ": 0.0 ,
      " duration ": 3.2 },
    {
      " text ": " It's been great, hasn't it? ",
      " start ": 3.2 ,
      " duration ": 2.9 }
  ]
} AI Agent Copy Pull the transcript from this TED talk and give me a bullet-point summary with key quotes get_transcript(video_url="dQw4w9WgXcQ") Here's the summary of "Do schools kill creativity?" by Sir Ken Robinson:

• Schools prioritize conformity over creative thinking
• Children are educated out of creativity as they age
• Key quote: "If you're not prepared to be wrong, you'll never come up with anything original"

